### 1.3 Department Head Role

**Tasks:**
- Add department_head role to User schema
- Department Head belongs to a city and a specific category (roads, water, sanitation, etc.)
- Mayor can create and assign Department Head accounts from their dashboard
- Department Head dashboard: scoped only to their category's issues in their city
- Department Head can: acknowledge issues, assign to contractors in their department, update status, sign off on field verification
- Department Head cannot: access other categories, broadcast city-wide, view other departments' scorecards
- Add Department Head to the issue assignment flow — Mayor assigns to Dept Head, Dept Head assigns to Contractor
- SLA alerts go to Department Head first, then escalate to Mayor if unacknowledged
- Department Head performance metrics appear in Mayor's scorecard view

---

### 1.4 Revised Issue Lifecycle

**Tasks:**
- Update Issue schema status enum: draft, submitted, under_triage, acknowledged, assigned, in_progress, field_verification, community_verified, closed, reopened
- Draft status: saved locally or in DB but not visible in public feed
- Under Triage: automatic 2-hour window after submission for triage jobs to run
- Assigned: new status set when contractor is explicitly assigned with contractor ID and timestamp
- Field Verification: contractor marks work complete, triggers notification to Department Head
- Community Verified: original reporter or verified citizens in radius confirm fix
- Closed: final state after verification
- Reopened: available within 30 days of closing if ghost audit or reporter flags recurrence
- Update all frontend status displays, filters, and badge colors for new statuses
- Update all backend route logic and cron jobs to handle new lifecycle
- Migration script for existing issues to map old statuses to new ones

